{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And the earth is profaned.</b> 'Torot': according to the balanced view, all humanity shared in it." "<b>They violated the statute.</b> Like 'cut off,' as in כליל יחלוף (Isaiah 2:18)." "<b>Statute.</b> They are the statutes of HaShem according to nature, and this is the meaning of 'everlasting covenant.'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "The gloss 'כרתו כמו כליל' equates חלפו with cutting off / passing away; the comparison to Isaiah 2:18 is rendered literally.", 2 "Reading התולדת as 'nature' (singular concept); could also be read as 'the generations.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:55.396414266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}